{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RNcJAu2DLbEUMmdNRJJE9g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 01: Movie list and day picker\n2\t\n3\t**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n4\t\n5\t**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n6\t\n7\t**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n8\t\n9\t**Status:** ready\n10\t\n11\t- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n12\t- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n13\t- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n14\t- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n15\t- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n16\t- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n17\t- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n18\t- [ ] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n19\t- [ ] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n20\t- [ ] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD