{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TKusarDGRbwJnvuFgfspLV","type":"tool_result","content":"# Stack\n\nThe workspace is an Nx 23 monorepo. The application is the Nx project `cinescope` in\n`apps/cinescope`, generated with the Nx Angular application generator: **Angular 22**,\nstandalone components, zoneless, Angular Router with an empty route list, SCSS, Vitest for\nunit tests and ESLint. **Angular Material 22** and the Angular CDK are installed, a Material\ntheme is applied in `styles.scss`, and the native date adapter is provided for the\ndatepicker. It is ready to run; build the application on top of it.\n----\n# Tickets\n\nWork through the tickets in order. A ticket can start once every ticket in its\n**Blocked by** line is done. The specification is [`../README.md`](../README.md); each\nticket names the sections it implements and the acceptance criteria it must satisfy.\n\n| # | Ticket | Blocked by | Criteria |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | [Movie list and day picker](01-movie-list.md) | — | 11 |\n| 02 | [Auditorium map](02-auditorium-map.md) | 01 | 13 |\n| 03 | [Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel](03-seat-selection.md) | 02 | 14 |\n| 04 | [Booking and summary](04-booking-summary.md) | 03 | 16 |\n| 05 | [Checkout and payment](05-checkout.md) | 04 | 13 |\n| 06 | [Confirmation and booking lifecycle](06-confirmation.md) | 05 | 2 |\n| 07 | [Final pass](07-final-pass.md) | 01–06 | all |\n\nA ticket is done when every box in it is ticked and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n----\n# 02: Auditorium map\n\n**What to build:** `/screenings/:id/seats` loads the screening and its movie and draws the page header (title, show date, seat-limit text), the `SCREEN` bar and the auditorium: 15 rows with row labels on both edges, both aisles in every row, the entrance gap in rows 1–10, accessible seats in row 1 and 12 couches in row 15. Occupied seats are shown as unavailable. Selection comes in ticket 03. An unknown screening id redirects to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.3, 5 (intro and layout), 5.1, 5.3 (colours of available, unavailable and accessible seats), 9.2, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 01 — Movie list and day picker.\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-05 — The seat map has 15 rows, numbered 1 to 15, row 1 rendered directly under the screen.\n- [ ] AC-06 — Rows 11 to 15 contain 24 columns; rows 1 to 10 contain columns 5 to 24 only.\n- [ ] AC-07 — A two-seat-wide gap is rendered between columns 4 and 5 and between columns 20 and 21 in every row; gaps carry no seat and no number.\n- [ ] AC-08 — Column numbering is global 1–24 and identical across rows; in rows 1–10, numbering starts at 5.\n- [ ] AC-09 — The row number is rendered on both the left and the right edge of every row.\n- [ ] AC-10 — Every seat renders its column number.\n- [ ] AC-11 — A `SCREEN` indicator is rendered above row 1.\n- [ ] AC-12 — Row 1, columns 10 to 15 are accessible seats — 6 of them.\n- [ ] AC-13 — Row 15 renders 12 couches, each spanning two adjacent columns: 1–2, 3–4, … 23–24.\n- [ ] AC-14 — A couch is rendered as one wide element, visually distinct from a single seat.\n- [ ] AC-15 — The total number of selectable elements in the auditorium is 308 (200 seats in rows 1–10, 96 in rows 11–14, 12 couches in row 15).\n- [ ] AC-56 — The seat selection shows the title `Choose your seats` and the subtitle `Show Date: <Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` of the screening.\n- [ ] AC-57 — Above the seat map, horizontally centred over it, the text `You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation` is shown.\n----\nspec:\nREADME.md\nstack.md\ntickets\n\nspec/tickets:\n01-movie-list.md\n02-auditorium-map.md\n03-seat-selection.md\n04-booking-summary.md\n05-checkout.md\n06-confirmation.md\n07-final-pass.md\nREADME.md\n674 spec/README.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01N31yniJEnfJFXEBbrc1PF1","session_id":"1e089a7a-4bad-4c15-8bdb-116c29d15f7d","uuid":"b9f9aec4-ff43-4fcb-a720-b33971193b2b","timestamp":"2026-11-27T11:58:07.868Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 02"}
