{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KEobUrTTSiHtvgX3DS9ZWH","type":"tool_result","content":"# 02: Auditorium map\n\n**What to build:** `/screenings/:id/seats` loads the screening and its movie and draws the page header (title, show date, seat-limit text), the `SCREEN` bar and the auditorium: 15 rows with row labels on both edges, both aisles in every row, the entrance gap in rows 1–10, accessible seats in row 1 and 12 couches in row 15. Occupied seats are shown as unavailable. Selection comes in ticket 03. An unknown screening id redirects to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 3.3, 5 (intro and layout), 5.1, 5.3 (colours of available, unavailable and accessible seats), 9.2, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 01 — Movie list and day picker.\n\n**Status:** done\n\n- [x] AC-05 — The seat map has 15 rows, numbered 1 to 15, row 1 rendered directly under the screen.\n- [x] AC-06 — Rows 11 to 15 contain 24 columns; rows 1 to 10 contain columns 5 to 24 only.\n- [x] AC-07 — A two-seat-wide gap is rendered between columns 4 and 5 and between columns 20 and 21 in every row; gaps carry no seat and no number.\n- [x] AC-08 — Column numbering is global 1–24 and identical across rows; in rows 1–10, numbering starts at 5.\n- [x] AC-09 — The row number is rendered on both the left and the right edge of every row.\n- [x] AC-10 — Every seat renders its column number.\n- [x] AC-11 — A `SCREEN` indicator is rendered above row 1.\n- [x] AC-12 — Row 1, columns 10 to 15 are accessible seats — 6 of them.\n- [x] AC-13 — Row 15 renders 12 couches, each spanning two adjacent columns: 1–2, 3–4, … 23–24.\n- [x] AC-14 — A couch is rendered as one wide element, visually distinct from a single seat.\n- [x] AC-15 — The total number of selectable elements in the auditorium is 308 (200 seats in rows 1–10, 96 in rows 11–14, 12 couches in row 15).\n- [x] AC-56 — The seat selection shows the title `Choose your seats` and the subtitle `Show Date: <Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` of the screening.\n- [x] AC-57 — Above the seat map, horizontally centred over it, the text `You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation` is shown.\n----\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core';\nimport { RouterOutlet } from '@angular/router';\n\n@Component({\n  imports: [RouterOutlet],\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  templateUrl: './app.html',\n  styleUrl: './app.scss',\n})\nexport class App {}\n<router-outlet />\nimport { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';\nimport { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\nimport { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';\nimport { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';\nimport { appRoutes } from './app.routes';\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(),\n    provideHttpClient(),\n    provideRouter(appRoutes),\n    provideNativeDateAdapter(),\n  ],\n};\nimport { Routes } from '@angular/router';\nimport { MovieList } from './movie-list/movie-list';\nimport { Placeholder } from './placeholder/placeholder';\nimport { SeatSelection } from './seat-selection/seat-selection';\n\nexport const appRoutes: Routes = [\n  { path: '', component: MovieList },\n  { path: 'screenings/:id/seats', component: SeatSelection },\n  { path: 'screenings/:id/summary', component: Placeholder },\n  { path: 'screenings/:id/checkout', component: Placeholder },\n  { path: 'confirmation', component: Placeholder },\n  { path: '**', redirectTo: '' },\n];\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core';\n\n/** Temporary screen for routes that later tickets implement. */\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-placeholder',\n  template: '',\n})\nexport class Placeholder {}\nimport { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\nimport { inject, Injectable } from '@angular/core';\nimport { Observable } from 'rxjs';\nimport { Movie, Screening } from './models';\n\nconst API_BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000';\n\n@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })\nexport class CinemaApi {\n  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);\n\n  getMovies(): Observable<Movie[]> {\n    return this.http.get<Movie[]>(`${API_BASE_URL}/movies`);\n  }\n\n  getScreenings(date: string): Observable<Screening[]> {\n    return this.http.get<Screening[]>(`${API_BASE_URL}/screenings`, { params: { date } });\n  }\n\n  getScreening(id: number): Observable<Screening> {\n    return this.http.get<Screening>(`${API_BASE_URL}/screenings/${id}`);\n  }\n\n  getMovie(id: number): Observable<Movie> {\n    return this.http.get<Movie>(`${API_BASE_URL}/movies/${id}`);\n  }\n}\nconst WEEKDAY_NAMES = ['Sunday', 'Monday', 'Tuesday', 'Wednesday', 'Thursday', 'Friday', 'Saturday'];\nconst MONTH_SHORT_NAMES = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];\n\n/** Local-calendar date at midnight for the current browser day. */\nexport function startOfToday(): Date {\n  const now = new Date();\n  return new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate());\n}\n\nexport function addDays(date: Date, days: number): Date {\n  return new Date(date.getFullYear(), date.getMonth(), date.getDate() + days);\n}\n\n/** Formats a date as `YYYY-MM-DD` using its local calendar fields. */\nexport function toIsoDate(date: Date): string {\n  const year = String(date.getFullYear()).padStart(4, '0');\n  const month = String(date.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, '0');\n  const day = String(date.getDate()).padStart(2, '0');\n  return `${year}-${month}-${day}`;\n}\n\n/** Parses a `YYYY-MM-DD` string into a local date at midnight. */\nexport function isoToDate(iso: string): Date {\n  const [year, month, day] = iso.split('-').map(Number);\n  return new Date(year, month - 1, day);\n}\n\n/** True for a well-formed ISO date that exists in the calendar (e.g. not 2026-02-30). */\nexport function isValidIsoDate(value: string | null): value is string {\n  if (value === null || !/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/.test(value)) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  return toIsoDate(isoToDate(value)) === value;\n}\n\nexport function weekdayName(date: Date): string {\n  return WEEKDAY_NAMES[date.getDay()];\n}\n\n/** The show date as `<Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>`, e.g. `Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00`. */\nexport function formatShowDate(isoDate: string, time: string): string {\n  const date = isoToDate(isoDate);\n  return `${weekdayName(date)} ${date.getDate()} ${MONTH_SHORT_NAMES[date.getMonth()]} ${time}`;\n}\nexport interface Movie {\n  id: number;\n  title: string;\n  genre: string;\n  runtimeMinutes: number;\n  format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles';\n}\n\nexport interface Screening {\n  id: number;\n  movieId: number;\n  date: string;\n  time: string;\n  occupiedSeats: string[];\n}\n----\nimport { Component, computed, effect, inject, resource } from '@angular/core';\nimport { toSignal } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';\nimport { ActivatedRoute, Router, RouterLink } from '@angular/router';\nimport { MatButton } from '@angular/material/button';\nimport { MatDatepickerModule } from '@angular/material/datepicker';\nimport { MatFormFieldModule } from '@angular/material/form-field';\nimport { MatInputModule } from '@angular/material/input';\nimport { firstValueFrom, forkJoin } from 'rxjs';\nimport { CinemaApi } from '../cinema-api';\nimport { addDays, isoToDate, isValidIsoDate, startOfToday, toIsoDate, weekdayName } from '../dates';\nimport { Movie, Screening } from '../models';\n\ninterface DayOption {\n  iso: string;\n  label: string;\n}\n\ninterface MovieCard {\n  movie: Movie;\n  screenings: Screening[];\n}\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-movie-list',\n  imports: [RouterLink, MatButton, MatDatepickerModule, MatFormFieldModule, MatInputModule],\n  templateUrl: './movie-list.html',\n  styleUrl: './movie-list.scss',\n})\nexport class MovieList {\n  private readonly api = inject(CinemaApi);\n  private readonly router = inject(Router);\n  private readonly route = inject(ActivatedRoute);\n\n  protected readonly today = startOfToday();\n  protected readonly todayIso = toIsoDate(this.today);\n\n  protected readonly days: DayOption[] = Array.from({ length: 5 }, (_, index) => {\n    const date = addDays(this.today, index);\n    return { iso: toIsoDate(date), label: index === 0 ? 'Today' : weekdayName(date) };\n  });\n\n  private readonly query = toSignal(this.route.queryParamMap, { requireSync: true });\n\n  /** The selected day: the `date` query parameter when it is a valid ISO date not before today, otherwise today. */\n  protected readonly selectedIso = computed(() => {\n    const requested = this.query().get('date');\n    return isValidIsoDate(requested) && requested >= this.todayIso ? requested : this.todayIso;\n  });\n\n  protected readonly pickerValue = computed(() => isoToDate(this.selectedIso()));\n\n  protected readonly data = resource({\n    params: () => this.selectedIso(),\n    loader: ({ params: date }) =>\n      firstValueFrom(\n        forkJoin({\n          movies: this.api.getMovies(),\n          screenings: this.api.getScreenings(date),\n        }),\n      ),\n  });\n\n  protected readonly cards = computed<MovieCard[]>(() => {\n    const data = this.data.value();\n    if (!data) {\n      return [];\n    }\n    return data.movies.flatMap((movie) => {\n      const screenings = data.screenings\n        .filter((screening) => screening.movieId === movie.id)\n        .sort((a, b) => a.time.localeCompare(b.time));\n      return screenings.length > 0 ? [{ movie, screenings }] : [];\n    });\n  });\n\n  constructor() {\n    // Replace an invalid or past `date` in the URL with the day that is actually shown.\n    effect(() => {\n      const requested = this.query().get('date');\n      const selected = this.selectedIso();\n      if (requested !== null && requested !== selected) {\n        void this.router.navigate([], { relativeTo: this.route, queryParams: { date: selected }, replaceUrl: true });\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  protected selectDay(iso: string): void {\n    void this.router.navigate([], { relativeTo: this.route, queryParams: { date: iso } });\n  }\n\n  protected onDatePicked(date: Date | null): void {\n    if (date !== null) {\n      this.selectDay(toIsoDate(date));\n    }\n  }\n}\n<main class=\"page\">\n  <div class=\"day-picker\" data-testid=\"day-picker\">\n    @for (day of days; track day.iso) {\n      @if (day.iso === selectedIso()) {\n        <button\n          mat-flat-button\n          type=\"button\"\n          data-testid=\"day-button\"\n          [attr.data-date]=\"day.iso\"\n          data-selected=\"true\"\n          (click)=\"selectDay(day.iso)\"\n        >{{ day.label }}</button>\n      } @else {\n        <button\n          mat-stroked-button\n          type=\"button\"\n          data-testid=\"day-button\"\n          [attr.data-date]=\"day.iso\"\n          data-selected=\"false\"\n          (click)=\"selectDay(day.iso)\"\n        >{{ day.label }}</button>\n      }\n    }\n\n    <mat-form-field subscriptSizing=\"dynamic\">\n      <mat-label>Other date</mat-label>\n      <input\n        matInput\n        data-testid=\"date-picker\"\n        [matDatepicker]=\"picker\"\n        [min]=\"today\"\n        [value]=\"pickerValue()\"\n        (dateChange)=\"onDatePicked($event.value)\"\n      />\n      <mat-datepicker-toggle matIconSuffix [for]=\"picker\" />\n      <mat-datepicker #picker />\n    </mat-form-field>\n  </div>\n\n  @if (data.isLoading()) {\n    <p class=\"status\" data-testid=\"movies-loading\">Loading…</p>\n  } @else if (data.error()) {\n    <div class=\"status\">\n      <p data-testid=\"movies-error\">Failed to load movies</p>\n      <button mat-flat-button type=\"button\" data-testid=\"movies-retry-button\" (click)=\"data.reload()\">Retry</button>\n    </div>\n  } @else if (cards().length === 0) {\n    <p class=\"status\" data-testid=\"movies-empty\">No screenings on this day</p>\n  } @else {\n    <div class=\"movie-list\" data-testid=\"movie-list\">\n      @for (card of cards(); track card.movie.id) {\n        <article class=\"movie-card\" data-testid=\"movie-card\" [attr.data-movie-id]=\"card.movie.id\">\n          <h2 data-testid=\"movie-title\">{{ card.movie.title }}</h2>\n          <p data-testid=\"movie-genre\">{{ card.movie.genre }}</p>\n          <p data-testid=\"movie-runtime\">{{ card.movie.runtimeMinutes }} min</p>\n          <p data-testid=\"movie-format\">{{ card.movie.format }}</p>\n          <div class=\"screenings\">\n            @for (screening of card.screenings; track screening.id) {\n              <button\n                mat-stroked-button\n                type=\"button\"\n                data-testid=\"screening-button\"\n                [attr.data-screening-id]=\"screening.id\"\n                [routerLink]=\"['/screenings', screening.id, 'seats']\"\n              >{{ screening.time }}</button>\n            }\n          </div>\n        </article>\n      }\n    </div>\n  }\n</main>\n----\n@use '@angular/material' as mat;\n\nhtml {\n  color-scheme: light;\n  @include mat.theme(\n    (\n      color: mat.$azure-palette,\n      typography: Roboto,\n      density: 0,\n    )\n  );\n}\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;\n}\n M apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts\n M apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts\n M spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md\n M spec/tickets/02-auditorium-map.md\n?? .pnpm-store/\n?? apps/cinescope/src/app/cinema-api.ts\n?? apps/cinescope/src/app/dates.ts\n?? apps/cinescope/src/app/models.ts\n?? apps/cinescope/src/app/movie-list/\n?? apps/cinescope/src/app/placeholder/\n?? apps/cinescope/src/app/seat-selection/\n17128d5 feat: scaffold app","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01H1BKzNkebJieUcj9asD2TB","session_id":"1e089a7a-4bad-4c15-8bdb-116c29d15f7d","uuid":"9387644b-144f-4047-9703-4b0b208bf9d7","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:00:17.033Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 03"}
