{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTQQsamuQVmQTCpb66Sv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GRmrpZfDxBThstteJ7PpZ3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 350,460p spec/README.md","description":"Read spec sections 6-8"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":26868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":711,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dk3Yyf8aLbHGBAC83iP4K9","session_id":"1e089a7a-4bad-4c15-8bdb-116c29d15f7d","uuid":"48237fb3-9866-43ef-9652-7ab57672f6b3","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:06:49.087Z","request_id":"req_011ChTQQsRc28mT1FuzPQhai","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 06"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GRmrpZfDxBThstteJ7PpZ3","type":"tool_result","content":"## 6. Summary (`/screenings/:id/summary`)\n\nThe screen loads the screening and its movie. If either cannot be loaded, redirect to `/`.\n\nA title `Your tickets`, then one list item per selected seat and one per selected couch,\nordered by row and then by column. Each item shows:\n\n| Field | Content | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| movie | the movie title | `The Silent Harbor` |\n| date and time | `<ISO date> <time>` of the screening | `2026-09-15 16:00` |\n| row | the row number | `7` |\n| seat | a seat: its column number; a couch: `Couch <a>-<b>` | `12` / `Couch 3-4` |\n| price | the price from 5.4 | `32.00 PLN` |\n| — | a `Remove` button | |\n\n`Remove` takes the seat or couch out of the booking; the list and the total update at\nonce. Removing the last item opens `/screenings/:id/seats`.\n\nBelow the list: `Total: <sum> PLN`, the sum of the listed prices with two decimals, e.g.\n`Total: 121.00 PLN`.\n\nTwo buttons side by side:\n\n- `Back` returns to `/screenings/:id/seats` with the selection intact.\n- `Confirm` opens `/screenings/:id/checkout`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Checkout (`/screenings/:id/checkout`)\n\nA title `Your details`, then a form with these fields. The labels of required fields end\nwith ` *`.\n\n| Field | Label | Required | Rule | Message when the rule fails |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| first name | `First name *` | yes | at least 2 characters | `First name must be at least 2 characters` |\n| last name | `Last name *` | yes | at least 2 characters | `Last name must be at least 2 characters` |\n| email | `Email *` | yes | a valid email address | `Enter a valid email address` |\n| confirm email | `Confirm email *` | yes | identical to Email | `Email addresses do not match` |\n| phone | `Phone number` | no | when filled: exactly 9 digits, nothing else | `Phone number must be exactly 9 digits` |\n| terms | `I accept the terms and conditions *` | yes | checked | `You must accept the terms and conditions` |\n\n- An empty required text field shows `<Label> is required`, with the label without the\n  asterisk, e.g. `First name is required` or `Confirm email is required`. A non-empty field\n  that breaks its rule shows the message from the table. At most one message per field.\n- A valid email address is: one or more characters without spaces or `@`, then `@`, then a\n  domain of characters without spaces or `@` that contains a dot with at least one\n  character on each side, e.g. `anna@example.com`. `not-an-email`, `a@b` and `a@.com` are\n  not valid.\n- Confirm email is compared with Email as typed, whether or not Email itself is valid.\n- Values are validated without trimming, except that an empty phone field is valid.\n- A field's message appears once the field has been left (blurred) at least once, and from\n  then on updates as the value changes. The terms checkbox counts as left once it has been\n  toggled. When the Email value changes, the Confirm email check is re-evaluated.\n\n### 7.1 Keeping the values\n\nThe six values are saved in the booking (section 3.1) as they are typed. Going `Back` to\nthe summary or the seat map and returning, or reloading the page, shows the same values.\nWhether a field was left is not saved: a restored form shows no messages until the\ncustomer leaves a field or clicks `Pay`.\n\n### 7.2 Buttons\n\nTwo buttons side by side: `Back` and the pay button.\n\n- `Back` returns to `/screenings/:id/summary` with the booking intact.\n- The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, e.g. `Pay 121.00 PLN`. It is enabled at all\n  times, except while a payment request is in flight.\n\nClicking the pay button:\n\n- **Invalid form** — marks every field as left, shows every failing message, shows the\n  toast `The form contains errors` and stays on the screen. No request is sent.\n- **Valid form** — sends `POST /reservations` (section 2.2) with the screening id, the\n  booked seat identifiers (in summary order, a couch as its two identifiers), the customer\n  data and the total price. While the request is in flight, the pay button is disabled and\n  reads `Processing…`.\n  - on success: the booking becomes paid, with the customer's email address, and\n    `/confirmation` opens;\n  - on failure: the screen stays as it is, with the values kept, the pay button becomes\n    enabled again and the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.` is shown.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Confirmation (`/confirmation`)\n\n- A heading `Payment successful`.\n- The text `Your tickets will be sent shortly to <email>`, with the email address from the\n  form.\n- A `Continue` button that clears the booking and opens `/`.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Element identifiers\n\nThe QA team's browser automation finds elements by the attributes below. Every element\nlisted must carry exactly this `data-testid` and the listed data attributes. Names and\nvalues are part of the contract: do not rename, abbreviate or prefix them, and do not put\nthese `data-testid` values on any other element.\n\n### 9.1 Movie list\n\n| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `day-picker` | container of the day buttons and the datepicker | — |\n| `day-button` | one of the five day buttons | `data-date`, `data-selected` |\n| `date-picker` | the datepicker | — |\n| `movie-list` | container of the movie cards | — |\n| `movies-loading` | loading indicator | — |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dk3Yyf8aLbHGBAC83iP4K9","session_id":"1e089a7a-4bad-4c15-8bdb-116c29d15f7d","uuid":"3ebb3c06-fcbc-4a1e-8468-5dbd8a3070b7","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:06:49.099Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 06"}
