{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTQQsamuQVmQTCpb66Sv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P3YtDbp3xT4gzBeM2qBbFX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 530,674p spec/README.md","description":"Read spec sections 9.5 onward and acceptance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":26868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":711,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dk3Yyf8aLbHGBAC83iP4K9","session_id":"1e089a7a-4bad-4c15-8bdb-116c29d15f7d","uuid":"72096430-e8b5-4a2f-9ba1-085499af88ba","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:06:49.324Z","request_id":"req_011ChTQQsRc28mT1FuzPQhai","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 06"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3YtDbp3xT4gzBeM2qBbFX","type":"tool_result","content":"| `email-error` | email message | — |\n| `confirm-email-error` | confirm email message | — |\n| `phone-error` | phone message | — |\n| `terms-error` | terms message | — |\n| `checkout-back-button` | `Back` | — |\n| `pay-button` | the pay button | — |\n\n### 9.5 Confirmation\n\n| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `confirmation-heading` | `Payment successful` heading | — |\n| `confirmation-message` | the `Your tickets will be sent shortly to …` text | — |\n| `confirmation-continue-button` | `Continue` | — |\n\n### 9.6 Any screen\n\n| `data-testid` | Element | Extra attributes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `toast` | the toast, containing its message text | — |\n\n### 9.7 Rules\n\n- `data-state` is exactly one of `available`, `selected`, `unavailable`, `accessible`. A\n  selected accessible seat reports `selected`; an occupied accessible seat reports\n  `unavailable`. Couches never report `accessible`.\n- `data-row`, `data-column`, `data-column-start`, `data-column-end`, `data-movie-id` and\n  `data-screening-id` hold plain numbers, e.g. `data-row=\"7\"`. `data-date` holds an ISO\n  date. `data-selected` is `true` or `false`.\n- `seat`, `couch` and `aisle` elements are inside their `seat-row` element.\n- A `seat` contains only its column number as text; a row label contains only the row\n  number; an `aisle` contains no text.\n- `summary-item-price` contains only the price, e.g. `32.00 PLN`; `summary-item-seat`\n  contains only the seat description, e.g. `12` or `Couch 3-4`; `summary-total` contains\n  only `Total: <sum> PLN`. `selected-seats-count` and each `selected-seats-row` contain only\n  their line.\n- **Library components.** The identifiers of the five text fields, the terms checkbox and\n  the datepicker may be placed either on the native `<input>` itself or on the\n  UI library's component element that contains it. Identifiers of buttons go on the\n  element that receives the click and is disabled when the button is disabled.\n- A field's `-error` element exists in the page only while its message is shown.\n- The `movies-loading` element exists in the page only while loading; `movies-empty` only\n  while the empty text is shown.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Acceptance criteria\n\nEach criterion is either met or not met.\n\n### Movie list\n- **AC-01** — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n- **AC-02** — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n- **AC-03** — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n- **AC-04** — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n- **AC-49** — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n- **AC-50** — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n- **AC-51** — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n- **AC-52** — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n- **AC-53** — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n- **AC-54** — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n- **AC-55** — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n\n### Auditorium geometry\n- **AC-05** — The seat map has 15 rows, numbered 1 to 15, row 1 rendered directly under the screen.\n- **AC-06** — Rows 11 to 15 contain 24 columns; rows 1 to 10 contain columns 5 to 24 only.\n- **AC-07** — A two-seat-wide gap is rendered between columns 4 and 5 and between columns 20 and 21 in every row; gaps carry no seat and no number.\n- **AC-08** — Column numbering is global 1–24 and identical across rows; in rows 1–10, numbering starts at 5.\n- **AC-09** — The row number is rendered on both the left and the right edge of every row.\n- **AC-10** — Every seat renders its column number.\n- **AC-11** — A `SCREEN` indicator is rendered above row 1.\n- **AC-12** — Row 1, columns 10 to 15 are accessible seats — 6 of them.\n- **AC-13** — Row 15 renders 12 couches, each spanning two adjacent columns: 1–2, 3–4, … 23–24.\n- **AC-14** — A couch is rendered as one wide element, visually distinct from a single seat.\n- **AC-15** — The total number of selectable elements in the auditorium is 308 (200 seats in rows 1–10, 96 in rows 11–14, 12 couches in row 15).\n- **AC-56** — The seat selection shows the title `Choose your seats` and the subtitle `Show Date: <Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>` of the screening.\n- **AC-57** — Above the seat map, horizontally centred over it, the text `You can reserve up to 10 seats per reservation` is shown.\n\n### Seat selection\n- **AC-16** — Seats listed in `occupiedSeats` for the screening are rendered unavailable and cannot be selected.\n- **AC-17** — A couch is unavailable when either of its two seat identifiers is in `occupiedSeats`.\n- **AC-18** — Clicking an available seat selects it; clicking it again deselects it.\n- **AC-19** — Clicking a couch selects both of its seats as one unit; it cannot be half-selected.\n- **AC-20** — Selection is capped at 10 seats; a couch counts as 2.\n- **AC-21** — A click that would exceed 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`.\n- **AC-22** — At the cap, already selected seats and couches can still be deselected.\n- **AC-58** — Between the seat map and the `Cancel` / `Continue` buttons, the selected-seats panel shows `Selected seats: <n>` and one `Row <r>: <seats>` line per row, updated on every selection change.\n- **AC-66** — Every seat-selection identifier in section 9.2, and the toast identifier in section 9.6, is present with the exact names and values given there.\n\n### Legend and colours\n- **AC-23** — The legend lists exactly `Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`.\n- **AC-24** — Available seats use `#2E7D32`.\n- **AC-25** — Selected seats use `#F9A825`.\n- **AC-26** — Unavailable seats use `#C62828`.\n- **AC-27** — Accessible seats use `#1565C0`.\n\n### Pricing\n- **AC-28** — Seats in rows 1–5 cost `25.00 PLN`.\n- **AC-29** — Seats in rows 6–10 cost `32.00 PLN`.\n- **AC-30** — Seats in rows 11–14 cost `39.00 PLN`.\n- **AC-31** — A couch costs `89.00 PLN` per couch, not per seat.\n- **AC-32** — Accessible seats cost `25.00 PLN`, like the rest of row 1.\n\n### Navigation from the seat map\n- **AC-33** — `Cancel` navigates to `/` and clears the selection.\n- **AC-34** — `Continue` navigates to `/screenings/:id/summary`.\n- **AC-35** — `Continue` does nothing when no seat is selected.\n\n### Summary\n- **AC-36** — Each selected item is listed with movie title, screening date, time, row number, seat description and price.\n- **AC-37** — A couch is described as `Couch <a>-<b>`; a single seat is described by its column number.\n- **AC-38** — The total line reads `Total: <sum> PLN` and equals the sum of the listed prices.\n- **AC-39** — `Back` returns to the seat map with the selection intact.\n- **AC-40** — `Confirm` navigates to `/screenings/:id/checkout`.\n- **AC-59** — The summary shows the title `Your tickets`.\n- **AC-60** — Each summary item has a `Remove` button that removes it from the booking and updates the total; removing the last item returns to the seat map.\n- **AC-67** — Every summary identifier in section 9.3 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n\n### Checkout\n- **AC-41** — The form renders first name, last name, email, confirm email, phone number and a terms checkbox.\n- **AC-42** — First name and last name are required and must be at least 2 characters.\n- **AC-43** — Email is required and must be a valid address; confirm email must match it.\n- **AC-44** — Phone number is optional; when filled it must be exactly 9 digits.\n- **AC-45** — The terms checkbox is required.\n- **AC-46** — The pay button is enabled whenever no payment request is in flight; clicking it on an invalid form marks all fields as touched, shows the messages and shows the toast `The form contains errors`, without navigating.\n- **AC-47** — The pay button on a valid form sends `POST /reservations`, is disabled while the request is in flight, navigates to `/confirmation` on success, and on failure stays on the form and shows the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.`\n- **AC-61** — The checkout shows the title `Your details`.\n- **AC-62** — The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, the total of the booking.\n- **AC-63** — `Back` on the checkout returns to the summary with the booking intact.\n- **AC-64** — The checkout values survive going back to the summary and forward again, and a page reload; a new booking starts with an empty form.\n- **AC-65** — The labels of the five required fields end with `*`; the phone label does not.\n- **AC-68** — Every checkout identifier in section 9.4 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n\n### Confirmation and booking\n- **AC-48** — `/confirmation` shows `Payment successful` and `Your tickets will be sent shortly to <email>`; `Continue` navigates to `/` and clears the booking; the booking survives a reload via `sessionStorage`; entering the summary, checkout or confirmation without a matching booking redirects to `/`.\n- **AC-69** — Every confirmation identifier in section 9.5 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Out of scope\n\nDo not build any of these: user accounts, real payment processing, seat locking between\nconcurrent customers, updating `occupiedSeats` after a reservation, posters or images,\nmobile or responsive layouts, keyboard navigation or ARIA beyond what the browser and\nthe UI library give by default, and translations.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dk3Yyf8aLbHGBAC83iP4K9","session_id":"1e089a7a-4bad-4c15-8bdb-116c29d15f7d","uuid":"f2d300a9-585a-48fc-b2b8-73656198eccf","timestamp":"2026-11-27T12:06:49.337Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement ticket 06"}
